    "text": "To determine how far a monkey will swing in 30 minutes, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Convert the time from minutes to seconds.\n2. Use the given average distance per second to calculate the total distance.\n\nFirst, we convert 30 minutes to seconds. Since there are 60 seconds in a minute, we have:\n\\[ 30 \\text{ minutes} \\times 60 \\text{ seconds/minute} = 1800 \\text{ seconds} \\]\n\nNext, we use the average distance the monkey swings per second, which is 1.2 meters per second. To find the total distance swung in 1800 seconds, we multiply the average distance per second by the total time in seconds:\n\\[ 1.2 \\text{ meters/second} \\times 1800 \\text{ seconds} = 2160 \\text{ meters} \\]\n\nTherefore, the total distance the monkey will swing in 30 minutes is:\n\\[ \\boxed{2160} \\]",
